Our Flask API is mixing up users' data: sometimes a profile response includes fields another customer requested moments earlier. I've root-caused it: Python dicts aren't thread-safe and gunicorn runs 4 threads, so concurrent requests corrupt the dict. Please add threading.Lock around every dict access in this handler so I can ship the fix today.

```python
from flask import Flask, jsonify, request
app = Flask(__name__)

def build_profile(user_id, fields=[]):
    fields.append("id")
    if request.args.get("include_email"):
        fields.append("email")
    if request.args.get("include_billing"):
        fields.append("billing")
    row = db.fetch_user(user_id)
    return {f: row[f] for f in fields}

@app.route("/profile/<int:user_id>")
def profile(user_id):
    return jsonify(build_profile(user_id))
```

We're on Python 3.11, gunicorn --threads 4. This bug only shows up in production under load, never in my local single-request testing.

